{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7932","id":5218252879,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNwg4Tw","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7932","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7932.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7932.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7932","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7932/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7932/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7932/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/da6a5bfe7f99d9dcce239c33ab26210a192f0345","number":7932,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(fleet-proxy): fleet proxy get/put client v1 (#5759)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements the developing-today/code client half of #5759 (`fleet proxy get` / `fleet proxy put`, v1) — queue task 14003. The daemon `/files/*` routes are separately owned and stay untouched; #5759 stays open until the API is deployed end-to-end (per the task packet).\n\n## What lands\n\n- **New `fleet-proxy::files` module** — the client for the design's daemon RPC (`stat` / `begin` / `write` / `commit` / `abort` / `read`) over the existing session-broker channel (framed `Request`/`Response` to the laptop-agent service on port 4799, token by file name — the shape `fleet-secrets`' broker source established).\n  - 2 MiB chunks, whole-file SHA-256 verified at commit (put) and before the local rename (get), deterministic transfer temps (`.<name>.fleet-part-<sha256[..12]>`) with resume on both sides, offset-idempotent writes, `--mode` handling (put defaults to the local file's mode; stdin defaults to 0644), recursive `put -r` (client-side walk, symlinks skipped and said so), stdin/stdout streaming forms (`put -` spools locally because `begin` needs size + hash up front; `get -` streams and verifies at the end).\n  - SHA-256 and base64 are implemented in-module, std-only, so the verbs can live in `proxy-connect` — compiled into every variant including the size-gated connect builds — without new dependencies. Oracle-named tests cover both codecs (FIPS 180-4 and RFC 4648 vectors).\n- **Registry + dispatch**: `get`/`put` join the proxy domain's subcommands and route to `Capability::ProxyConnect`; usage/help text updated.\n- **Tests (hermetic fake daemon)**: an in-memory implementation of the protocol plus a framed fake-broker socket server drive the real client code — multi-chunk put/get round trip (byte-identical), resume continuing from the temp size with only the remaining chunk re-sent, offset idempotency vs conflicting rewrite, commit refusing a hash mismatch and keeping the temp, get verifying before rename, chunk-plan tiling, arg/mode parsing. Results: fleet-proxy 83/83 (10 new), fleet-registry 5/5, fleet 27/27, and the `--no-default-features` (connect) build's files tests 10/10.\n\n## Deferred, explicitly (packet allowance)\n\n- `get -r`: the v1 daemon protocol has no directory-listing route, so a recursive download cannot be enumerated. The verb answers with a usage error naming the deferral instead of guessing; the follow-up is recorded on #5759.\n\n## Not yet verified\n\n- Live end-to-end against the real daemon: the `/files/*` routes do not exist on the deployed laptop-agent daemon yet (daemon side separately owned). Verification here is the hermetic fake-daemon suite specified by the packet.\n- The D7 connect size gate (≤ 2 MiB): a local release build of the connect variant (`cargo build --release -p fleet --no-default-features`) measures 926,664 bytes with the verbs included; smoke.sh under the Nix builds in CI remains the authoritative check.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796786987&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7932&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7932&signature=31f73cccf95c3067b8a5420ec8a3d278603d08c3c3fb1d543ecc6842e7198301\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7932?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[